       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Endpoint: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "https://open.canada.ca/data/api/3/action/"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " · Why it matters: NRCan, Transport Canada, StatCan, rail network"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Not-yet-investigated"
   },
   "children": [
    "Not yet investigated"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Listed so the gap is explicit rather than silently absent:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "**Burlington, St. Catharines, Welland, Niagara Falls, Thorold, Port"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Colborne, Grimsby, Lincoln, Fort Erie",
    {
     "children": [
      "* — municipal portals not yet probed. Burlington matters most; it is in the core scope and is "
     ],
     "tag": "em"
    },
    "not* covered by either the Hamilton or the Niagara Region datasets above."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Halton Region"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Burlington's upper tier; may publish employment land."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Statistics Canada"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — business counts by NAICS and CSD; useful for"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "validating the NEI and for the Hamilton business gap."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Port of Hamilton / HOPA Ports"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — returned HTTP 403 to a plain request on"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "2026-08-18; needs a different approach or a human look."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "St. Lawrence Seaway"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — ",
      {
       "children": [
        "seaway-greatlakes.com/vessel-transit"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " is public"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "and server-rendered, ",
    {
     "children": [
      "but ",
      {
       "children": [
        "robots.txt"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " is ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Disallow: /"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ". Do not build an automated collector against it. Link out instead. (Already established while building the main site's Ships board.)"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "CN / CPKC / Metrolinx / VIA"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — public infrastructure data not yet sought."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Assume no freight positions; see the note below."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Brownfields"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Hamilton has a brownfield programme; a spatial dataset was"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "not obvious in the DCAT scan and needs a targeted search. OSM currently supplies 263 ",
    {
     "children": [
      "landuse=brownfield"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " polygons region-wide as an interim proxy."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Hamilton \"Industrial Sectors A–N\""
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — the City names its industrial"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "districts on its neighbourhood boundaries map (a PDF, not a dataset: ",
    {
     "children": [
      "map.hamilton.ca/Static/PDFs/General Interest maps/Overall City/"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "). Relevant to §14 corridor detection as the authoritative naming to check discovered clusters against."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Known-dead-ends"
   },
   "children": [
    "Known dead ends"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Recorded so they are not re-attempted:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "No public real-time freight rail feed exists in Canada."
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " CN and CPKC do"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "not publish train positions; shipment tracking is customer-authenticated. Static rail infrastructure is available and is sufficient for Layers 1–3, as the brief anticipates. This was established independently while building the Ships board."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Seaway vessel transit data"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ": public to read, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Disallow: /"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " to crawl."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Niagara ArcGIS Hub DCAT feed"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ": 404 at ",
      {
       "children": [
        "/api/feed/dcat-us/1.1.json"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". Use"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "the CKAN catalogue at ",
    {
     "children": [
      "niagaraopendata.ca"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " for discovery instead."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "MPAC (Municipal Property Assessment Corporation)"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " is the obvious place to"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "look for Ontario parcel and property-assessment data, and it is a paid dead end: bulk access is fee-based and income/expense data is withheld. There is no Ontario equivalent of the UK rating-list feed that underpins the standard academic method for detecting industrial underuse. Noted so it is not re-investigated. (Established independently in ",
    {
     "children": [
      "babbworks/clark-dot-babb"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", Track 2.)"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Constraint-on-derived-&quot;underuse&quot;-labels"
   },
   "children": [
    "Constraint on derived \"underuse\" labels"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The atlas can observe that OSM records a building as disused, or that a polygon is tagged brownfield. It cannot conclude that a named business is underperforming, that a site is vacant today, or that an owner is neglecting a property — those are claims about identifiable people and companies, and publishing them wrongly is a legal problem, not just a data-quality one."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Rules for anything in this class, including the §11 connectivity score and any future vacancy layer:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Publish observations, not judgements."
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " \"OSM records this building as"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "disused, last edited <date>\" is an observation. \"This site is underutilized\" is a judgement."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Date-stamp everything"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ", and show the date next to the claim."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Derive labels only from cited public records"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ", never from inference over"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "several sources that individually say less."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Provide an owner correction path"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " before publishing anything at"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "property level."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Consider tiered detail."
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " Precise vacancy information has misuse value —"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "squatting, metal theft, title fraud. A public heatmap with detail reserved for verified partners is the established mitigation, and it also serves brief rule 15."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The ",
    {
     "children": [
      "osm-disused"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " layer is deliberately named ",
    {
     "children": [
      "\"Brownfield & recorded disused\""
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " rather than \"underutilized\" for exactly this reason, and its features carry the category ",
    {
     "children": [
      "DISUSED (RECORDED)"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " — recording what the source says, not what we conclude."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Gaps-and-what-they-imply"
   },
   "children": [
    "Gaps and what they imply"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "1. There is no Hamilton equivalent of the NEI."
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " Niagara publishes 98,065 classified business points; Hamilton publishes building footprints, zoning and employment land, but no comparable business inventory. The first version of the atlas will therefore be ",
    {
     "children": [
      "asymmetric by construction"
     ],
     "tag": "em"
    },
    ": business-level detail in Niagara, building- and land-level detail in Hamilton."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "This must be visible in the UI. A user seeing dense business points across Niagara and sparse ones across Hamilton would reasonably conclude Hamilton has less industry, which is false — it is a data artefact. Options, in preference order:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Show per-layer coverage explicitly, per §16 freshness states."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Lean on OSM for Hamilton business-level points, clearly attributed."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Investigate Hamilton's \"Businesses by Employee Count\" layer to see whether"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "it is point-level or aggregated to areas."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "2. Licence mixing needs a decision before publishing derived data."
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " OSM is ODbL (share-alike), Hamilton is a bespoke municipal licence, Niagara is OGL 2.0. A derived layer combining all three — the industrial density heatmap, for example — needs the compatibility question answered deliberately, not discovered after publication."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "3. Layer indices are unstable."
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " Resolve by dataset name via the catalogue feeds at build time."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Prioritization"
   },
   "children": [
    "Prioritization"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Scored against the brief's criteria. Implementation cost is relative."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Niagara Consolidated NEI"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★★★ · Freshness: ★★★ · Coverage: Niagara only · Authority: ★★★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★★★ · Cost: Low"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Hamilton Employment Lands"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★★★ · Freshness: ★★★★ · Coverage: Hamilton only · Authority: ★★★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★★ · Cost: Low"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Hamilton Buildings"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★★ · Freshness: ★★★★ · Coverage: Hamilton only · Authority: ★★★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★★ · Cost: Medium (214k features)"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Hamilton Zoning"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★★ · Freshness: ★★★★ · Coverage: Hamilton only · Authority: ★★★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★★ · Cost: Low"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Hamilton Railways"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★★ · Freshness: ★★★ · Coverage: Hamilton only · Authority: ★★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★★ · Cost: Low"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "OSM / Overpass"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★★ · Freshness: ★★★★★ · Coverage: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Whole region"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " · Authority: ★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★ (ODbL) · Cost: Low"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Hamilton Truck Routes"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Value: ★★★ · Freshness: ★★★ · Coverage: Hamilton only · Authority: ★★★★★ · Machine-readable: ★★★★★ · Licence: ★★★★ · Cost: Low"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Recommended first build order:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " OSM (region-wide backbone) → Hamilton Employment Lands + Zoning (land) → Niagara NEI (business) → Hamilton Buildings (physical fabric) → Hamilton Railways + OSM rail (corridors) → derived density."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Reference-implementation"
   },
   "children": [
    "Reference implementation"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "babbworks/atlas"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (branch ",
    {
     "children": [
      "master"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", last pushed 2026-06-10) — \"Discover workshops, manufacturing sites, and industrial spaces across the UK — Leaflet + OSM/Overpass\". No licence file."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Its shape confirms the pipeline this brief describes: a static Leaflet app (",
    {
     "children": [
      "app.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " 85KB, ",
    {
     "children": [
      "map.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " 21KB, ",
    {
     "children": [
      "overpass.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " 7KB, ",
    {
     "children": [
      "styles.css"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " 46KB) over ",
    {
     "children": [
      "pre-generated JSON in ",
      {
       "children": [
        "data/"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " built by Python scripts in ",
    {
     "children": [
      "scripts/"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", with per-source modules (",
    {
     "children": [
      "voa.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "children": [
      "epr.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "children": [
      "fsa.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "children": [
      "planning.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "children": [
      "companies.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ") and a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "scoring.js"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " for derived indicators. Large datasets are split by key into ",
    {
     "children": [
      "data/voa/*.json"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " to keep fetches small — a pattern worth copying for 214k Hamilton buildings."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "It also keeps ",
    {
     "children": [
      "system/datasets.md"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "children": [
      "system/project-notes.md"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", which is the same instinct as this document."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Reproducing-this-reconnaissance"
   },
   "children": [
    "Reproducing this reconnaissance"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "# Hamilton catalogue\ncurl -s https://open.hamilton.ca/api/feed/dcat-us/1.1.json -o ham_dcat.json\n\n# Any Hamilton layer's record count\ncurl -s \"https://services.arcgis.com/rYz782eMbySr2srL/arcgis/rest/services/Employment_Lands/FeatureServer/2/query?where=1=1&returnCountOnly=true&f=json\"\n\n# Niagara catalogue search (CKAN)\ncurl -s \"https://niagaraopendata.ca/api/3/action/package_search?q=NEI&rows=10\"\n\n# NEI schema\ncurl -s \"https://services1.arcgis.com/WxiLK82TWf8W3O3f/arcgis/rest/services/OpenData_Consolidated_NEI_Opendata/FeatureServer/45?f=json\"\n\n# Overpass probe\ncurl -s -X POST https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter \\\n  --data-urlencode 'data=[out:json][timeout:50];(way\"landuse\"=\"industrial\";);out count;'"
   ],
   "tag": "pre"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Prepared with Claude (Anthropic) · model Claude Opus 5.5 · 2026-11-18"
     ],
     "tag": "em"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
